        "text": "Is a signature with Email OTP an AES? No. It is still an SES. The one-time code proves that the person who opened the agreement controlled the email inbox at that moment, which strengthens your evidence, but it doesn't give the signer a certificate or bind the signature cryptographically to them. Ask for SignatureLevel…"
